# Packages hyprconf adds to a fresh Omarchy install.
#
# Official Arch repositories ONLY — see the no-AUR policy in AGENTS.md. Omarchy
# ships yay and uses the AUR itself, but hyprconf does not reach for it.
#
# Installed via `omarchy-pkg-add`, which is idempotent (guards with
# omarchy-pkg-missing, verifies with `pacman -Q`). Never call `pacman -Syu`
# here: Omarchy installs an ALPM AbortOnFail hook that blocks sysupgrade forms.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed — already in Omarchy's own base:
#   eza zoxide fastfetch starship yay ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd-basic
#   xdg-terminal-exec foot

# Terminal. Becomes Omarchy's default via `omarchy-default-terminal`.
kitty

# Font. Geist Mono is the retro-modern face hyprconf sets as the system
# monospace on first install; the -nerd build carries the full Nerd Font glyph
# set the bar widgets draw from. Omarchy's own ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd-basic
# stays installed and remains selectable with `omarchy font set`.
otf-geist-mono-nerd

# Shell. hyprconf runs zsh inside kitty while leaving the LOGIN shell as bash,
# so Omarchy's own bash rc chain, session and scripts are untouched.
zsh
zsh-autosuggestions
zsh-syntax-highlighting

# Keybind dependencies — hypr/bindings.lua launches these and a fresh
# Omarchy ships none of them.
#
# hyprshot was here for SUPER+SHIFT+4. That key now calls Omarchy's own
# `omarchy-capture-screenshot region`, which freezes the screen the same way
# (hyprpicker -r -z) and adds the click-to-edit notification back.
#
# playerctl was here for the media keys. Those now go to Omarchy's own
# `omarchy-shell media`, and nothing else wants it: no Omarchy binary invokes
# playerctl, and its shell only matches the *string* "playerctld" as a D-Bus
# name to recognise that player. An orphan package is not a free one.
firefox     # SUPER+F
code        # SUPER+C
# NB: SUPER+E is deliberately NOT dolphin here — it is repointed at Omarchy's
# own nautilus rather than pulling a chunk of KDE onto an Omarchy system.
